URL:https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/events/ceenrg-seminars-climate-change-nationa
 l-courts-promising-route
CATEGORIES:Law,Policy
DESCRIPTION:Faculty of Law\nTopics: Law\, Policy\nDetails: https://www.law.
 cam.ac.uk/events/ceenrg-seminars-climate-change-national-courts-promising-
 route\nSign-up needed: https://forms.office.com/e/K4QaYcz4mi\nProfessor An
 dreas Paulus (Professor\, Chair of Public and International Law\, Universi
 ty of Göttingen)\n\n Date/time: \n\n Thursday 26 November 2026 \n\n 3:00p
 m to 4:00pm\n\n Location: \n\n David Attenborough Building\, Room 1.25\n\n
  Open map \n\n About \n\n Climate change litigation has made its way from 
 domestic courts to international courts. Of the former\, some have refused
  to reign in parliaments\, others have established long-term constitutiona
 l duties towards the younger and future generations\, inter alia the need 
 to cooperate rather than freeride\, the budget approach to figure out a fa
 ir burden-sharing. International Courts have followed suit\, demanding a j
 udicial control of climate legislation for future generations\, espousing 
 the concept of rights of nature\, clarifying the climate goal\, the differ
 entiated State responsibility\, and the customary nature of reduction duti
 es. The speaker\, who served a
END:VEVENT
